## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design edge routing with policy-driven gating and cross-DC deployment, plus observability and security concerns in docker-dca.

## Key Concepts

- TLS termination at the edge with Nginx
- Central policy engine (OPA) integration
- Per-tenant feature flag evaluation
- Cross-DC routing semantics
- Observability with Prometheus and OTEL

## Code Example

```rego
package featureflag.allow
default allow = false
allow {
  input.tenant == "tenant-A"
  input.flag == "new_feature"
}
```

```nginx
# Nginx map-based routing example
http {
  map $http_x_feature_flag $upstream {
    default http://api_v1;
    "new_feature" http://api_v2;
  }
  server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    location /api/ { proxy_pass $upstream; }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement cache invalidation for policy decisions?
- How would you test the canary routing?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of per-tenant routing, docker configs, and zero-downtime reconfiguration in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Traefik dynamic config and weighted routing
- Docker Configs for per-tenant policy
- TLS termination at edge proxy
- Multi-DC docker-dca deployment basics
- Observability of per-tenant routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Traefik dynamic config snippet (example)
{
  "http": {
    "routers": {
      "tenant-ab": {
        "rule": "Host(`api.local`)",
        "tls": { "certResolver": "myresolver" },
        "service": "ab-backend"
      }
    },
    "services": {
      "ab-backend": {
        "loadBalancer": {
          "weighted": {
            "services": [
              { "name": "api-v1", "weight": 80 },
              { "name": "api-v2", "weight": 20 }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant weight changes in production?
- How would you handle missing or malformed ab-split entries?
- How would you monitor skew and rollback strategies?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design distributed feature-flag propagation with per-tenant isolation across data centers. It covers Docker Config for tenant flags, per-tenant in-process caching with TTL, Redis Pub/Sub for invalidation and cross-DC propagation, and edge security with TLS termination at Traefik.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for tenant-specific flag storage
- Per-tenant in-process cache with configurable TTL
- Redis Pub/Sub for cache invalidation and propagation
- Lightweight policy/flag service coordinating across DCs
- TLS termination at Traefik edge proxy

## Code Example
```javascript
class FlagCache {
  constructor(redis, ttlSeconds = 120) {
    this.cache = new Map();
    this.ttlSeconds = ttlSeconds;
    this.redis = redis;

    redis.subscribe('tenant-flags', (err, count) => {
      if (err) console.error('Subscribe error:', err);
    });

    redis.on('message', (channel, message) => {
      if (channel === 'tenant-flags') {
        const { tenantId } = JSON.parse(message);
        this.cache.delete(tenantId);
      }
    });
  }

  async getFlag(tenantId, feature) {
    const key = `${tenantId}:${feature}`;
    const entry = this.cache.get(key);

    if (entry && Date.now() < entry.expiresAt) {
      return entry.value;
    }

    const value = await this.redis.hget(`flags:${tenantId}`, feature);
    this.cache.set(key, { value: JSON.parse(value), expiresAt: Date.now() + this.ttlSeconds * 1000 });
    return JSON.parse(value);
  }
}
```
